      <div type="clause" n="5.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 5.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="286" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.2"/> mæssepreost<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.16"/> æfre ahwær<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.17"/> stande on leasre gewitnesse oððe on mænan aðe oððe þeofa gewita oððe gewyrhta beo, þonne sy he aworpen of gehadodra gemanan ⁊ þolige ægþer ge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.1"/> geferscipes ge freondscipes ge æghwylces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.2"/> weorðscipes, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.3"/> he wið God ⁊ wið menn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.4"/> þe deoplicor gebete, swa bisceop<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.5"/> him tæce, ⁊ him borh finde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he þanon forð æfre swylces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.2"/> geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="286" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif mæssepreost æfre ahwer stande on leasre gewittnesse oððe on mænan aðe oððe þeofa gewita oððe gewyrhta beo, þonne sy he aworpen of gehadodra gemanan ⁊ þolige ægðer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.1-4"/> geferscipes ge freondscipes ge æghwilces weorðscipes, buton he wið Godd ⁊ wið menn þe deoplicor gebete, swa biscop him tæce, ⁊ him borh finde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he þanon forð æfre swilces geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="286" ed="#liebermann"/>Si sacerdos aliquando<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.12"/> falsus testis uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.13"/> periurus extiterit uel furtum fecerit uel in aliquo consenserit, deponatur et omni<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.1-2"/> bonorum societate<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.2-2"/>, dilectione careat et honore, si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.3-2"/> non erga Deum et homines dignis penitentię fructibus secundum episcopi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.4-2"/> sui iussionem preparetur ad ueniam, et emendationis et legalitatis plegios deinceps inueniat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="287" ed="#liebermann"/>Presbyter si calumniatus et conuictus fuerit, quod stetisset in falso testimonio aut iurasset<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.1-3"/> cum periuris<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.2-3"/> aut fuisset socius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.3-4"/> aut conscius latrocinii<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.4-3"/>, deponatur á communione et á societate ordinatorum et careat liberalitate<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.5-2"/> eorum, quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.6"/> Angli uocant þegenscipe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.7"/>, nisi profundius satisfaciat Deo et hominibus secundum pręceptum episcopi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.8"/> sui, et fideiussores inueniat, quod ab eo tempore amplius cessabit ab eiusmodi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.oe.9"/> operibus.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="287" ed="#liebermann"/>Si uero presbiter de falso testimonio uel periurio siue furto uel furti conscientia conuictus fuerit, ab ordinatorum consortio degradetur, careatque tam societate quam amicitia uniuersoque honore, nisi erga Deum et erga homines emendauerit, secundum quod episcopo uisum fuerit, fideiussoremque, se in posterum a tali crimine inmunem fore, dederit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="5a.3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="160" ed="#robertson"/>And gyf mæssepreost æfre ahwær stande on leasre gewitnesse oððe on mænan aðe oððe ðeofa gewita oððe gewyrhta beo, þonne sy he aworpen of gehadodra gemanan ⁊ þolige ægþer ge geferscipes ge freondscipes ge æghwylces weorðscipes, butan he wið God ⁊ wið menn þe deoplicor gebete, swa bisceop him tæce, ⁊ him borh finde þæt he þanon forð æfre swylces geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="238" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf mæssepreost æfre ahwær stande on leasre gewitnesse oððe on mænan aðe oððe þeofa gewita oððe gewyrhta beo, þonne sy he aworpen of gehadodra gemanan and þolige ægþer, ge geferscipes, ge freondscipes ge æghwylces weorðscipes, butan he wið God and wið menn þe deoplicor gebete, swa bisceop him tæce, and him borh finde þæt he þanon forð æfre swylces geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="287" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn ein Priester je irgendwo in falschem Zeugniss oder im Meineid [ertappt] dasteht, oder Mitwisser von Dieben oder Mitwirker ist, dann sei er verstossen aus Gemeinschaft der Geistlichen und verliere sowohl [deren] Genossenschaft wie Freundschaft und jeden Ehrenrang<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.de.1"/>, ausser<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_5-3.lnote.de.2"/> wenn er gegenüber Gott und Weltlichen um so tiefer büsst, wie [sein] Bischof ihm vorschreibt, und Bürgschaft für sich findet [dafür], dass er stets hinfort von solchem [Verbrechen] ablassen werde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if a priest anywhere stands [convicted] of false witness or perjury, or is an accessory or accomplice of thieves, then let him be cast out of the fellowship of the clergy and lose both [their] fellowship and friendship and every honour, unless he makes all the deeper amends before God and men, as [his] bishop prescribes for him, and finds surety [to the effect] that he will forever desist from such [crimes].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#missing"/><pb n="161" ed="#robertson"/>And if a priest anywhere be concerned in false witness or perjury, or be the accessory and accomplice of thieves, he shall be cast out from the fellowship of those in holy orders and shall forfeit both their society and their friendship and every kind of privilege, unless he make amends, both towards God and towards men, to the utmost of his ability, as the bishop shall prescribe for him, and find surety that henceforth he will cease for ever from all such [wrong-doing].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="239" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If a priest is anywhere guilty of bearing false witness or committing perjury or being the aide or accomplice to thieves, then he is to be expelled from holy orders and deprived of companionship, friendship, and all entitlements unless he repents most deeply to God and the community entirely as the bishop instructs, and finds surety that he thenceforth will cease all wrongdoing.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="287"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_27">VIII Atr 27</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 27</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_36-1">II Cn 36.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="93"><label>=</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_27">VIII Atr 27</ref> <quote>VIII Atr 27 = I Cn 5:3</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann supplies ‘ge’ in A. Liebermann compares VIII Atr 27.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 287, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
